            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Soup Loving Nicole"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tender, flavorable, and simple. This is a basic that you can use by itself or add things to suit your taste. I added some chili powder and ceyenne for extra kick but this is a great starter recipe. The tequila and lime tenderize and the honey carmelized and sealed in the additional flavors. I even used a cheap tequila we had sitting around for years and I was very impressed with the results. If you like the lime to shine through, use extra."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bonnie Silverman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "After reading all of the reviews, I doubled the lime juice, honey and cumin. I then added salt, lime zest and cayenne pepper. I only marinated for 1.5 hour and because It was raining, I had to use a grill pan and finish it in oven. Besides my husband complaining that it smelled like body odor, it tastes very good and the recipe used things that I always have in the house.",
